## 1. Creating Strings

Strings are sequences of characters enclosed within single, double, or triple quotes.

```python
name = "Vihari"
language = 'Python'

print(name)
print(language)
```

---

## 2. String Indexing

Each character in a string has an index starting from `0`.

```python
text = "Python"

print(text[0])    # P
print(text[2])    # t
print(text[-1])   # n
```

---

## 3. String Slicing

Slicing is used to extract a specific portion of a string.

```python
text = "Python Programming"

print(text[0:6])
print(text[:6])
print(text[7:])
print(text[::-1])
```

---

## 4. Common String Methods

Python provides several built-in methods for manipulating strings.

```python
text = "python programming"

print(text.upper())
print(text.lower())
print(text.title())
print(text.capitalize())
print(text.replace("python", "Java"))
```

### Frequently Used Methods

| Method         | Purpose                         |
| -------------- | ------------------------------- |
| `upper()`      | Converts to uppercase           |
| `lower()`      | Converts to lowercase           |
| `title()`      | Converts to title case          |
| `capitalize()` | Capitalizes first character     |
| `replace()`    | Replaces text                   |
| `strip()`      | Removes leading/trailing spaces |
| `split()`      | Splits a string                 |
| `join()`       | Joins strings                   |

---

## 5. Searching in Strings

The `in` operator and `find()` method can be used to search for text.

```python
text = "Python is easy to learn"

print("Python" in text)
print(text.find("easy"))
```

---

## 6. Splitting and Joining

### Split

```python
text = "Python,Java,C++"

languages = text.split(",")

print(languages)
```

### Join

```python
languages = ["Python", "Java", "C++"]

result = " - ".join(languages)

print(result)
```

---

## 7. String Formatting

F-strings provide a simple way to insert variables into strings.

```python
name = "Vihari"
skill = "Python"

print(f"My name is {name} and I am learning {skill}.")
```

---

## 8. String Validation

Python provides methods to check the contents of a string.

```python
text = "Python123"

print(text.isalpha())
print(text.isdigit())
print(text.isalnum())
print(text.startswith("Python"))
print(text.endswith("123"))
```

